          { name: "Partisan Ideology as a Substitute for Constituent Service", tag: "avoid", why: "A district at $75,357 income with 36.3% college attainment and a 44-year median age is fundamentally pragmatic about governance: voters in this district care whether schools are funded, whether roads are maintained, whether healthcare is accessible and affordable, and whether housing is achievable — not whether the legislator can deliver the most ideologically pure performance for a partisan base. Any representative whose legislative focus is primarily on national partisan culture-war issues or abstract conservative positioning rather than the material conditions of working professionals, families, renters, and educated constituents will find that positioning increasingly costly in a district where 100% opposition is mathematically possible if a capable challenger emerges and offers a more responsive alternative." }
