          "Address renter and younger-adult housing affordability directly: at $73,925 median household income with 19.1% renters, the rental population is likely below-median earners facing affordability stress, and the low 15.2% college-attainment rate signals limited economic mobility pathways — these are material concerns amenable to specific policy responses.",
          "Develop a workforce and education strategy that reflects local opportunity rather than defaulting to abstract market rhetoric: the 15.2% college-attainment rate suggests either limited education infrastructure or communities skeptical of traditional higher education's relevance; a representative who understands local workforce needs and can articulate how education policy serves them builds more durable constituent support.",
          "Treat an unopposed 2024 result as an absence-of-opposition signal, not a stability signal: in a safely Republican district, the absence of a challenger may reflect limited Democratic resources or candidate recruitment rather than certainty that no credible alternative could emerge; active constituent engagement now prevents vulnerability to a well-resourced challenger in a future cycle."
