          "Maintain college-educated voter alignment on institutional competence and governance: the 60.3% college attainment rate signals a constituency that evaluates on professional competence, institutional norms, and whether government is functioning effectively — not tribal or minority-rights issues. This is an educated, professional constituency that votes Democratic for competence and policy, not identity-based mobilization.",
          "Invest heavily in turnout operations targeting renters and young adults: the 65.1% renter rate and 25.5 median age indicate a mobile, transient constituency with lower propensity to vote in midterm or off-year elections. In a state with strong Republican turnout infrastructure, aggressive Democratic field organizing in this district is not optional — it is the difference between holding 63% and losing to Republican turnout advantage.",
